Skip the item merge event when nothing is listening.

CraftEventFactory#callItemMergeEvent built two CraftEntity casts, an ItemMergeEvent and a
plugin-manager dispatch on every item merge. The event can only cancel the merge, so with no
listener registered the method always returns true - returning it directly is exactly equivalent.

Item merging runs continuously wherever drops pile up: mob farms, mining, mass drops. It is called
from ItemEntity#mergeWithNeighbours, which itself runs from the item's tick.

--- a/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/event/CraftEventFactory.java
+++ b/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/event/CraftEventFactory.java
@@ -843,6 +843,10 @@
     public static boolean callItemMergeEvent(ItemEntity merging, ItemEntity mergingWith) {
+        // AtlasSpigot - the event can only veto; with no listener the answer is always true
+        if (ItemMergeEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length == 0) {
+            return true;
+        }
         org.bukkit.entity.Item entityMerging = (org.bukkit.entity.Item) merging.getBukkitEntity();
